{"solve_log_md": "# Solve Log — airport_gate_assignment (integrated_terminal_day_slice)

## Commands
1. `python /app/submissions/solve.py` (run from scratch; reads `/app/data/*`, writes `/app/submissions/solution.csv`).

## Model summary
- Sets: 28 flights, 12 gates, 10 connections, 6 rotations, 2 adjacent-conflict pairs, 2 MARS pairs, taxiway meters, handler/facility capacities.
- Variables:
  - `x[f,g]` binary: flight f to gate g (only for class/region-compatible gates).
  - `y[f]` binary: flight f to remote apron (only if not must_contact_gate).
  - `z[c,g1,g2]` binary: connection c with both flights on gates g1,g2.
  - `wa[c]`, `wb[c]` binary: connection c with inbound/outbound on apron.
  - `e[c]` continuous: noncritical connection walk excess.
- Constraints: assignment (one of gate/apron), gate overlap (robust intervals), turnaround extra buffers (pairwise gate reuse), adjacent safety conflicts, MARS combined-envelope conflicts, rotations (same gate + min turn, verified feasible in data), apron capacity 3 (time-point sweep), remote bank limits (1 per bank), handler capacities (total + wide-body per bank), security/immigration/remote-bus capacities, taxiway metering, connection walk (critical enforced, noncritical excess variable).
- Objective: minimize walk cost (arr*baggage + dep*security) + 1.4*connection walk + 8*taxi + 550*priority*terminal mismatch + (1800 + 4*pax)*apron + 20*excess.

## Solver settings
- SCIP via PySCIPOpt, `gaprel = 0.0005`, time limit = `ORCLAW_SOLVE_TIME_LIMIT_SECONDS` if set (else 300s).

